The current frontend uses a copy of `accommodations.geojson` and contains 13,120 real accommodation records. It is not yet a complete restaurant, hospital, supermarket or general business dataset.

### 2.3 Routing

| Area | Container | Port | Graph directory |
|---|---|---:|---|
| Ho Chi Minh City | `osrm-hcm` | 5000 | `Routing-HCM` |
| Hanoi | `osrm-hanoi` | 5001 | `Routing-Hanoi` |
| Da Nang | `osrm-danang` | 5002 | `Routing-Danang` |

Each routing directory contains one complete OSRM MLD graph. Files sharing the `.osrm.*` prefix form one graph and must not be edited or replaced individually.

### 2.4 Frontend

```text
D:\Bản đồ VN\LifeFlow\map-app
```

The current frontend provides:

- MapLibre map rendering
- OpenFreeMap basemap
- Pan, zoom and navigation controls
- HCM, Hanoi and Da Nang switching
- POI clustering and popup details
- Search over the current POI dataset
- A/B selection and OSRM routing
- Route geometry, distance and estimated duration
- Desktop and mobile layouts

The startup script is:

```text
D:\Bản đồ VN\LifeFlow\Start-LifeFlow.ps1
```

## 3. Core design principles

1. MCP is an interface for agents, not a database.
2. PostgreSQL with PostGIS is the system of record for LifeFlow business and spatial data.
3. OSRM remains the routing engine; routing algorithms will not be rewritten.
4. MapLibre remains the renderer.
5. Basemap, routing and business POI are independent layers.
6. Raw OSM files and generated OSRM graphs are immutable build inputs and artifacts.
7. LifeFlow custom data must survive every OSM update.
8. An LLM must never receive unrestricted SQL access.
9. Tools that spend money or change state require explicit user approval.
10. Every write operation must be auditable and idempotent.
11. Housing search performs factual, deterministic filtering; recommendation remains a separate downstream responsibility.

## 4. Target architecture

```text
User
  |
  v
LifeFlow Web / Mobile
  |-- Dashboard, chat and workflow UI
  |-- MapLibre map
  |
  v
LifeFlow Platform API
  |-- Place and housing services
  |-- Workflow and approval services
  |-- Integration adapters
  |
  +------------------+------------------+
  |                  |                  |
  v                  v                  v
PostgreSQL/PostGIS   OSRM               External providers
                    routing            transport, health, flight
  ^
  |
LifeFlow MCP Server
  ^
  |
LifeFlow Agent / LLM
```

### 4.1 Runtime responsibility

| Component | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| MapLibre frontend | Render map, POI, route, selections and workflow results |
| Platform API | Authentication, validation and reusable business services |
| MCP server | Expose safe tools, resources and prompts to agents |
| PostgreSQL/PostGIS | Store canonical places, housing, workflows and spatial data |
| OSRM | Calculate routes, distance and duration |
| Object storage | Store images and large media files |
| Workers | Import OSM, synchronize providers and run background jobs |

The frontend should call the Platform API, not PostgreSQL or MCP directly. The MCP server should reuse the same application services as the Platform API instead of duplicating business logic.

